The Systems Hall (corona): an underground bunker installation with an armoured embankment,
an access trench open to the sky with the illusion of a gradual descent underground,
a pressurised armoured hatch recessed at z=0 with a clear inner hall,
the monumental lavender neon sign "SALA SISTEMI",
neon/black checkered anti-intrusion barriers, security pillars with lights rotating in 8 directions,
an access barrier arm, industrial ventilation grilles and a geodesic radar dome on the roof.
Written by Gemini CLI (Gemini 3.8 Flash, subscription) on 23/10/2026, task T19.
Box: 14 × 14 × 5 tiles, 112 × 112 × 40 voxels, 8 voxels per tile.
Key letters:
  O = door (letter O, name "porta", at the centre x=56, y=36..37, z=0..16, an armoured hatch with an empty inner through hall)
  F = sign ("SALA SISTEMI", lavender neon b9a6ff with a steady glow on two lines above the armoured hatch on the back wall at z=18..29)
  P = dark matte plate for the sign
  M = primary cybernetic black metal (14141a, armour, lintels, pilasters, ribs)
  m = dark secondary metal (20222a, protective casings, technical panelling, frames, flanges)
  C = graphite concrete and composite (363842, retaining walls of the trench, bases)
  c = dark asphalt aggregate and technical paving (282a32, road surface of the trench)
  G = geotextile cover / dark camouflage bunker grass (354a32, embankment)
  g = dark shaded cover (283826, steps and slopes of the embankment)
  S = light steel (8a8f9c, fall-protection handrails and railings, tie rods, light cages, radar stem)
  s = dark structural steel (525662, joining profiles, ventilation grilles, channels)
  V = dark reflecting glass (181c28, geodesic radar panels)
  v = cold bluish reflections of the radar (2c3848)
  w = lavender reflections of the radar (403858)
  N = bright lavender accent neon (b9a6ff glow, frames, checkered barriers, warnings)
  n = soft lavender neon (7a66b8 glow, ground guide of the trench, sub-grilles, radar ring)
  R = red obstacle light on top of the antenna (ff3a3a glow)
  x = temporary buffer for the animation (hidden)
Phases of the rotating light (1..8):
  1 = main active beam (b9a6ff glow) pointing in one of the 8 cardinal/intercardinal directions.
  8 = phosphor decay trail (8a70c8 glow) on the previous sector.
  7 = residual fade without glow (504270).
  2..6 = darkened lens, off (221e2c).
Architecture:
  - A stepped armoured perimeter embankment (x=10..102, y=10..102, z=0..26) in graphite concrete and camouflage geotextile.
  - A central trench open to the sky (x=45..67, y=36..104, z=0) with a technical asphalt floor at z=0.
  - Side retaining walls rising gradually from z=3 at the entrance to z=26 at the back, creating the illusion of going down deep.
  - The trench widens to x=43..69 at the back (y=36..42) to give visual room to the hatch and to the plate of the sign.
  - Steel fall-protection railings on the upper edge of the trench.
  - Armoured hatch O centred at z=0 with an empty inner hall over 16 voxels deep (y=18..35).
  - The sign "SALA SISTEMI" on two lines centred at x=56 above the hatch on the north wall of the trench, perfectly readable.
  - Entrance checkpoint to the south (y=96..104): lavender/black checkered jersey barriers, two security pillars with rotating lights and an access barrier arm.
  - A geodesic radar radome (x=20..36, y=18..32, z=24..37) with a neon scan ring on the west plateau of the bunker.
  - An industrial ventilation station with louvred cooling grilles and extraction rotors (x=70..88, y=18..34, z=24..28) on the east plateau.
Animation "rotazione" (8 frames):
  A cyclic, synchronised 360° rotation of the strobe alarm/guide lights on top of the two security pillars.
-->
